Used in deterministic, two-player, zero-sum games. MAX picks the move with the maximum minimax value, MIN picks the minimum. Values propagate from leaves (utilities) to the root.
MINIMAX(s):
    if TERMINAL(s): return UTILITY(s)
    if player(s) == MAX: return max over a of MINIMAX(RESULT(s,a))
    if player(s) == MIN: return min over a of MINIMAX(RESULT(s,a))
• Complete (finite tree), optimal against an optimal opponent.
• Time O(b^m), space O(bm) with DFS.
• Impractical for chess → use depth cut-off with evaluation function.

Let A = {a:0.3, b:0.7, c:1.0} and B = {a:0.6, b:0.4, c:0.5}.
Union          max : {a:0.6, b:0.7, c:1.0}
Intersection   min : {a:0.3, b:0.4, c:0.5}
Complement of A    : {a:0.7, b:0.3, c:0.0}
